        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "fcdded15-2234-3366-b29f-5fc2eb85d576",
                "word": "ostensiblement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bc7bf5f5-4dcb-3e82-b3c2-cb59f4950afd",
                        "entry_id": "fcdded15-2234-3366-b29f-5fc2eb85d576",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D'une manière qui vise à être vue, ou simplement de manière visible."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "21f7906c-f6be-44b9-8f37-8946b38f8221",
                                "sense_id": "bc7bf5f5-4dcb-3e82-b3c2-cb59f4950afd",
                                "text": "Ostensiblement, il prit un manille noir comme du charbon dont il cracha le bout par terre avant de l’allumer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f215c28-8705-42bf-819f-9b3da43220e7",
                                "sense_id": "bc7bf5f5-4dcb-3e82-b3c2-cb59f4950afd",
                                "text": "Lorsque l’on eut fini, sous le prétexte des fatigues de la journée, on se sépara pour se livrer ostensiblement au repos, mais en réalité pour être seul et réfléchir aux événements de la journée."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4990561-2595-4220-99dc-2d67a3317302",
                                "sense_id": "bc7bf5f5-4dcb-3e82-b3c2-cb59f4950afd",
                                "text": "À la porte, se trouvaient Phellion et Sébastien, les seuls qui dans ce grand désastre particulier osassent rester ostensiblement fidèles à cet accusé."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb63b785-141f-40ea-8e4d-7763f3d21d0b",
                                "sense_id": "bc7bf5f5-4dcb-3e82-b3c2-cb59f4950afd",
                                "text": "« Considérant que M. Durot , maire de la commune d’Antheny, se livre ostensiblement dans sa commune à une propagande active en faveur du candidat hostile au gouvernement du maréchal, suspend M. Durot de ses fonctions. »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31f08d83-e70e-4646-bc0e-0e4dc0f0f334",
                                "sense_id": "bc7bf5f5-4dcb-3e82-b3c2-cb59f4950afd",
                                "text": "Le 15 mars 2004, … le législateur français vote une loi interdisant, dans les écoles, collèges et lycées publics, les signes et les tenues qui manifestent ostensiblement une appartenance religieuse."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "66f4b50c-b197-4e58-8f04-addda186ea8a",
                        "source_entry_id": "fcdded15-2234-3366-b29f-5fc2eb85d576",
                        "source_sense_id": "bc7bf5f5-4dcb-3e82-b3c2-cb59f4950afd",
                        "target_lang_word": "ostensibly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ostensibly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                        "entry_id": "021a4e3d-de2c-3c8a-8f0c-d17fccecd405",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Seemingly, apparently, on the surface; supposedly, according to representations or implications made by someone (especially when their motives are suspected by others)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "modal",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4fc5b64-97fc-42b3-ab06-41af404febc3",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: reportedly, reputedly, purportedly, putatively, rumoredly, supposedly, allegedly, possibly, probably, likely, plausibly, presumably; see also Thesaurus:ostensibly"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f811d5c3-378a-4ef2-bfa0-22c3c73cd8bc",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "His interest in the railway was ostensibly a hobby, but people began wondering why he was taking photos of specific trains and specific equipment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e061cf7-0185-4848-9258-fab346deceb9",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "Her interest in his welfare was ostensibly charitable and magnanimous, but people began wondering who was going to inherit his assets when he died."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2595348-57d3-4dba-8d68-e83655857d58",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "On 13 June the peshwa signed a new treaty, ostensibly complying with the demands of the British government[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccc2cce4-663f-41fd-9ea3-a2d570de6a81",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "Up to a year or two ago it had been the custom to kill horses in the yards — ostensibly for fertilizer; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cba2f9f-6b16-4fc1-a5e3-12d0cb3d04be",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "The original branch was 5¾ miles long, from Llantrisant to Cowbridge only, but in 1889, the T.V.R. [Taff Vale Railway] obtained powers […] to continue the line for 6½ miles south to the coast at Aberthaw, ostensibly for the purpose of serving the important limestone works there, but one suspects other motives, including an understandable desire on the part of the T.V.R. to put a spoke in the wheel of the oncoming Barry Railway !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "950007ee-bbc7-4a99-bdcc-fcc4485734ad",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "People strive to achieve perfection — ostensibly an honorable goal — but complete perfection is dangerous. To be imperfect, but human, is far preferable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ada8001e-0878-4433-ab20-29f62c90d8c8",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "Mr. Marwan’s story — a tale overflowing with the suspense and ruthless duplicity of a spy novel — began to take shape in the spring of 1969. He had come to London, ostensibly to consult a Harley Street doctor about a stomach ailment. He chose to be examined by a doctor whose offices had been used previously for a covert meeting between King Hussein of Jordan and the general director of the Israeli prime minister’s office.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74ed80ff-2ffc-4f84-8519-9485b33147a2",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "The \"petrol clams\" are fleshy and flavourful -- the secret to avoiding a hydrocarbon taste is not to inhale while slipping them into the mouth -- and a speciality of the West Sea Barrage beach at Nampho, southwest of Pyongyang.\nThe sandy beach lies at the far end of the eight-kilometre barrier across the Taedong river mouth -- ostensibly built for flood control, but which also blocks access to Pyongyang, a few dozen kilometres upriver, for any invading navy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14e79710-77ce-43c6-838e-520ec0438d91",
                                                "sense_id": "857d1493-533a-3a7a-8479-f2031fce625d",
                                                "text": "Quite possibly the worst aspect of this is the role of the train operating companies and their representative body, the ineptly named Rail Delivery Group (RDG). Ostensibly, the plan has come from them. In reality, this has been driven entirely by Government, which asked each train operator to draw up plans for its area."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
